WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.440
Movie

00:01.440 --> 00:08.240
From Pythagoras to Godel. Have you ever contemplated how the abstract world of numbers and equations came into existence?

00:09.200 --> 00:17.280
It's a captivating tale one that has seen mathematics evolve into an intricate system over centuries in this vast timeline

00:17.760 --> 00:25.080
The dawn of mathematical thought can be traced back to the early civilizations who used rudimentary calculations for trade and astronomy

00:25.680 --> 00:29.840
Among these early thinkers a figure of paramount importance emerged

00:30.920 --> 00:32.000
Pythagoras

00:32.000 --> 00:41.080
This Greek philosopher and mathematician known for his eponymous theorem laid the groundwork for future explorations in geometry and number theory

00:42.240 --> 00:47.640
Pythagoras's theorem a fundamental principle in geometry states that in a right angled triangle

00:47.880 --> 00:52.920
The square of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides

00:53.520 --> 00:59.720
This theorem still taught in classrooms today represents one of the earliest instances of mathematical proof

01:00.120 --> 01:04.960
So with Pythagoras the foundation of mathematics took a significant leap forward

01:04.960 --> 01:10.400
But the journey was only beginning as centuries passed mathematicians built upon these foundations

01:10.600 --> 01:18.120
Leading to more complex theories and systems the story of mathematics is a tale of continuous evolution an unending quest for knowledge that

01:18.240 --> 01:22.040
Started with the geometric proofs of Pythagoras and carried on through the ages

01:22.600 --> 01:26.640
After Pythagoras we saw the emergence of mathematical luminaries like Euclid

01:26.840 --> 01:32.280
Whose elements served as the cornerstone for geometry and Archimedes who pioneered the concept of limits

01:32.680 --> 01:37.800
we witnessed the brilliance of Isaac Newton and Gottfried Leibniz in the 17th century as

01:38.040 --> 01:43.640
They independently invented calculus a field that has since become integral to the physical sciences

01:44.200 --> 01:50.040
In the 19th century, we were introduced to non Euclidean geometry by Nikolai Lobachevsky and Janos Bolyai

01:50.680 --> 01:57.600
Challenging our preconceived notions about the nature of space and then came the set theory from Georg Cantor

01:57.880 --> 02:06.360
Which revolutionized our understanding of infinity as we entered the 20th century a new figure emerged on the mathematical stage Kurt Godel

02:07.000 --> 02:11.800
Godel an Austrian logician made groundbreaking contributions to the field of mathematics

02:12.040 --> 02:17.320
He challenged the very foundations of logic and set theory creating ripples that are felt even today

02:17.760 --> 02:20.600
Godel is best known for his incompleteness theorems

02:20.680 --> 02:24.120
The first theorem states that in any consistent formal system

02:24.120 --> 02:27.480
There are statements that cannot be proven or disproven within the system

02:27.520 --> 02:32.040
The second theorem asserts that a system cannot demonstrate its own consistency

02:32.040 --> 02:39.720
These theorems shook the world of mathematics raising philosophical questions about truth proof and the limits of human knowledge

02:40.800 --> 02:46.600
Godel's work essentially told us that there are truths in mathematics that are true, but unprovable

02:47.240 --> 02:54.500
It revealed the inherent limitations of formal systems and by extension the limitations of human comprehension

02:55.240 --> 03:01.360
Godel's work thus reshaped our understanding of mathematics proving that there will always be more to discover

03:01.920 --> 03:08.120
His theorems remind us that the journey of mathematical thought is far from over and like the Grand Cathedral's of old

03:08.280 --> 03:11.720
The edifice of mathematics is still under construction

03:11.880 --> 03:17.880
It's pinnacle reaching towards the infinite from the geometry of Pythagoras to Godel's abstract logic

03:18.120 --> 03:20.920
These mathematical giants have left a profound legacy

03:21.560 --> 03:25.960
With Pythagoras we find ourselves rooted in tangible geometric realities

03:26.280 --> 03:29.960
His theorem is a cornerstone in the edifice of Euclidean geometry

03:30.440 --> 03:38.040
It's a testament to the power of deduction a bridge connecting the abstract world of numbers to the concrete world of shapes and spaces

03:38.760 --> 03:43.000
From the sides of a right-angled triangle to the orbits of celestial bodies

03:43.560 --> 03:48.760
The echoes of the Pythagorean theorem resonate in every corner of our spatially bound existence

03:49.400 --> 03:55.400
Contrast this with Godel whose incompleteness theorems plunge us deep into the realm of abstract logic

03:55.880 --> 03:57.880
He showed us that within any given system

03:58.600 --> 04:04.360
There are truths that cannot be proven using the rules of that system. It's a startling revelation

04:04.760 --> 04:09.080
A paradoxical twist that challenges our very understanding of truth and proof

04:09.880 --> 04:18.280
His work has far-reaching implications stretching beyond mathematics and into the heart of philosophy computer science and even artificial intelligence

04:19.000 --> 04:24.120
Both Pythagoras and Godel have left indelible marks on the tapestry of human knowledge

04:24.520 --> 04:31.880
Their theories have shaped our understanding of the universe from the minutiae of geometric relationships to the abstract complexities of logical systems

04:32.360 --> 04:39.240
They've influenced various fields from physics where Pythagoras's theorem underpins the laws of motion to computer science

04:39.560 --> 04:47.480
Where Godel's theorems guide our understanding of computation and complexity and their legacy extends beyond their specific contributions

04:47.880 --> 04:56.440
They've inspired countless mathematicians and scientists sparking curiosity fostering creativity and driving the relentless pursuit of knowledge

04:57.080 --> 05:00.380
Their work reminds us that mathematics is more than a tool for calculation

05:01.020 --> 05:06.780
It's a language for understanding the universe a lens through which we can glimpse the fundamental truths of reality

05:07.420 --> 05:11.740
In the grand narrative of mathematics the contributions of Pythagoras and Godel

05:12.220 --> 05:20.060
Serve as significant milestones reminding us that the journey of discovery is endless and the beauty of mathematics lies in its eternal quest for truth

